:: Robin Cafe Widgets [widget]
/* Shown when the player discusses the stand while Robin also works at the cafe. */
<<widget "robinCafeNotice">>
	<<run ensureRobinCafe()>>
	<<if robinCafeEmployed()>>
		<br>
		"I work at the cafe during the week now, so I only run the stand at weekends," Robin says while wiping the counter.
		<<if $robinCafe.lastWage gt 0>>
			"Sam paid me <span class="gold">£<<print $robinCafe.lastWage>></span> last week. I put it with the money from the stand."
		<<else>>
			"The cafe doesn't pay much yet, but at least I know how much I'll earn each week."
		<</if>>
		<br><br>
		<span class="blue">Robin now earns cafe wages during the week, but the stand only makes money at weekends.</span>
	<</if>>
<</widget>>

/* Cafe conversations the player can start at the orphanage. */
<<widget "robinCafeOptions">>
	<<run ensureRobinCafe()>>
	<<if robinCafeTellAvailable()>>
		<<cafeicon>><<link [[Tell Robin about the cafe job (0:15)|Robin Cafe Tell]]>><<pass 15>><</link>>
		<br>
	<<elseif robinCafeResolutionAvailable()>>
		<<cafeicon>><<link [[Ask Robin about the cafe (0:15)|Robin Cafe Decision]]>><<pass 15>><</link>>
		<br>
	<</if>>
	<<robinOutfitOptions>>
<</widget>>

:: Robin Cafe Ask Sam
<<endevent>>
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "cafe">><<effects>>
<<npc Sam>><<person1>>
<<run ensureRobinCafe()>>
You wait until there are no customers at the counter before speaking to Sam.
"A friend?" Sam asks. "How old?"
<br><br>
You tell <<him>> Robin's age. Sam thinks for a few seconds before answering.
"Same age as you, then. Can <<nnpc_he "Robin">> work weekday afternoons?"
<br><br>
You say yes.
<br><br>
Sam turns towards the work rota pinned beside Old Betsy. Several afternoon shifts still have nobody assigned to them.
"I could use the help. But <<nnpc_he "Robin">> needs to handle customers. Some of them get rude when they're angry or impatient."
 <br><br>
<<if $speech_attitude is "bratty">>
	"<<nnpc_He "Robin">>'ll be fine," you say. "<<nnpc_He "Robin">> can handle that."
<<elseif $speech_attitude is "meek" or $speech_attitude is "shy">>
	"<<nnpc_He "Robin">> works harder than anyone I know," you say quietly.
	"<<nnpc_Hes "Robin">> been running a drinks stand alone since <<nnpc_he "Robin">> was small."
<<else>>
	You tell Sam about Robin's drinks stand, explaining how <<nnpc_he "Robin">>
	sells lemonade in warm weather and cocoa in winter.
	You also mention that <<nnpc_he "Robin">> makes <<nnpc_his "Robin">> own signs and serves the customers alone.
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Robin Cafe Ask Sam 2]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Robin Cafe Ask Sam 2
<<effects>>
Sam listens with <<his>> arms folded. By the time you finish, <<he>> is smiling.
"<<nnpc_He "Robin">> runs <<nnpc_his "Robin">> own stall already?"
<br><br>
Sam thinks about it, then nods. "Bring <<nnpc_him "Robin">> in. I'll give <<nnpc_him "Robin">> two weeks to try the job.
If <<nnpc_he "Robin">> does well, <<nnpc_he "Robin">> can stay."
<br><br>
<<He>> points towards the tables. "And tell <<nnpc_him "Robin">> that any tips customers give <<nnpc_him "Robin">>
are <<nnpc_his "Robin">> to keep. We don't share tips between the staff here."
<br><br>
<span class="gold"><i>Sam has a place for Robin. You need to tell Robin about it.</i></span>
<<set $robinCafe.stage to 1>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Ocean Breeze]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: Robin Cafe Tell
<<endevent>>
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "home">><<effects>>
<<npc Robin>><<person1>>
<<run ensureRobinCafe()>>
You tell Robin what Sam said. <<He>> listens without interrupting, unusually quiet.
<br><br>
"A real job," <<he>> says when you finish. "I'd get paid every week, and I'd know which days I'm working."
<br><br>
<<He>> sits on the edge of the bed and looks down at <<his>> hands.
"I've been trying to work out the money while you were talking. We'd still be okay. I know that."
<br><br>
<<He>> rubs <<his>> palms against <<his>> knees.
"But what if I'm bad at it?"
<br><br>
<<if $speech_attitude is "bratty">>
	"Then you'll be bad at it for two weeks and Sam'll tell you," you say. "That's why <<he>> gave you a trial."
<<elseif $speech_attitude is "meek" or $speech_attitude is "shy">>
	"You've been working on your own since you were nine," you say. "You can learn this too."
<<else>>
	"Then you'll learn," you say. "That's what the two-week trial is for."
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Robin Cafe Tell 2]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Robin Cafe Tell 2
<<effects>>
Robin stays quiet for a few seconds, then starts counting the days on <<his>> fingers.
"Only weekdays... So I can still run the stand at weekends."
<br><br>
<<He>> looks up at you.
"I wouldn't have to give it up."
<br><br>
Robin pushes <<himself>> to <<his>> feet so quickly that <<he>> loses <<his>> balance.
<<He>> grabs the bedframe with one hand and steadies <<himself>>.
<br><br>
"Okay," <<he>> says. "Tell Sam yes."
<br><br>
<<He>> pauses, then shakes <<his>> head.
<br><br>
"No. I'll tell <<nnpc_him "Sam">> myself. I should do that."
<<npcincr Robin love 2>><<npcincr Robin dom 2>><<glove>><<ggdom>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Robin Cafe Tell 3]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Robin Cafe Tell 3
<<effects>>
<span class="gold">Robin starts work at the Ocean Breeze on the next school day</span>, from five until seven.
<br><br>
Robin will spend less time at the stand during the week, <span class="purple">so the stand will earn less money.</span>
<<set $robinCafe.stage to 2>><<set $robinCafe.startTime to Time.date.timeStamp>>
<br><br>
<<robinoptions>>

:: Robin Cafe Visit
<<endevent>>
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "cafe">><<effects>>
<<npc Robin>><<person1>>
<<run ensureRobinCafe()>>
<<set _due to robinCafeSceneDue()>>
<<set _outfitDue to robinOutfitSceneDue()>>
<<if _due is "first">>
	<<link [[Next|Robin Cafe First Shift]]>><</link>>
<<elseif _due is "difficult">>
	<<link [[Next|Robin Cafe Difficult]]>><</link>>
<<elseif _outfitDue is "debut">>
	<<link [[Next|Robin Outfit Debut]]>><</link>>
<<elseif _outfitDue is "regulars">>
	<<link [[Next|Robin Outfit Regulars]]>><</link>>
<<else>>
	<<if robinOutfitWorn()>>
		<<robinOutfitLook>>
	<<else>>
		Robin stands behind the counter wearing an apron that is too long for <<him>>.
		Sam has folded it over twice at the waist to make it fit.
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	<<if $robinCafe.stage gte 5 and $robinCafe.ended is "kept">>
		Robin takes a customer's order, passes it to the kitchen, then collects two empty plates on
		<<his>> way back to the counter. <<He>> moves from one job to the next without stopping.
		<br><br>
		<<He>> spots you while carrying the plates and gives you a quick grin before continuing back to the counter.
	<<elseif $robinCafe.stage gte 3>>
		Robin serves the last few people in a short queue, pressing each order into the till
		before moving straight to the next customer.
		<br><br>
		When the queue is gone, <<he>> comes over to you while the coffee machine prepares another drink behind <<him>>.
		"Eleven tables since five! I counted."
	<<else>>
		Robin is staring at the till, checking each button before pressing it.
		<<He>> does not notice you until you reach the counter.
		<br><br>
		When <<he>> looks up and sees you, <<he>> forgets which part of the order <<he>> was entering.
		<<He>> looks back at the screen and starts it again from the beginning with flushed cheeks.
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	<<if !$daily.robin.cafeVisit>>
		<<set $daily.robin.cafeVisit to 1>>
		Robin places a drink in front of you even though you did not order anything.
		"Staff discount! On me. I get one every shift and I never use it."
		<<stress -6>><<lstress>><<npcincr Robin love 1>><<glove>>
		<br><br>
	<<else>>
		Robin keeps moving between the till and the waiting orders.
		You decide not to distract <<him>> while <<he>> is working.
		<br><br>
	<</if>>
	<<robinOutfitOptions>>
	<<link [[Leave <<him>> to it|Ocean Breeze]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>

:: Robin Cafe First Shift
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "cafe">><<effects>>
<<run ensureRobinCafe()>>
<<set $robinCafe.seen.first to true>>
You find Robin carrying two plates while four customers wait near the counter.
A third plate is ready beside Sam, but Robin keeps looking between the food in <<his>> hands and the table numbers.
<br><br>
Sam prepares another order behind the counter.
"Table six!" Sam calls.
<br><br>
Robin quietly repeats the number to <<himself>> while walking away.
<br><br>
"Two coffees for table three!" Sam calls after <<him>>.
<br><br>
Robin looks back, loses track of what <<he>> was repeating, then turns towards the nearest occupied table.
<<He>> sets both plates down.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Robin Cafe First Shift 2]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Robin Cafe First Shift 2
<<effects>>
One of the customers looks at the food. "We didn't order these."
<br><br>
Robin freezes, then quickly picks the plates back up.
"Sorry. Sorry..."
<br><br>
<<He>> turns towards the other tables, but stops after a few steps.
<<He>> looks down at the two plates and moves one slightly in <<his>> hand, trying to remember which order belongs where.
<br><br>
<<if C.npc.Robin.dom gte 40>>
	Robin carries both plates back to the counter and puts them down.
	<<He>> takes a slow breath, then returns to the customers.
	<br><br>
	"Sorry. Which one was yours?" <<he>> asks.
	<br><br>
	The customers point out their order. Robin checks the plates again, then carries the right one back to them.
	<br><br>
	When <<he>> returns, <<he>> stares at the remaining plate for a second, surprised that asking actually solved the problem.
<<else>>
	Robin's ears turn red. <<He>> brings both plates back to the counter and puts them down beside Sam.
	<br><br>
	"Sorry," <<he>> says again, though nobody has spoken to <<him>>.
	<br><br>
	Sam checks the plates, points towards the correct tables, and sends <<him>> back out.
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Robin Cafe First Shift 3]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Robin Cafe First Shift 3
<<effects>>
The rush slowly dies down. Fewer customers are waiting now, and Robin finally has a chance to stop moving.
<br><br>
<<He>> comes over to you after clearing another table. There is an empty chair beside you, but <<he>> remains standing.
<br><br>
"That was awful," <<he>> says. "...I was awful."
<br><br>
<<if $speech_attitude is "bratty">>
	"You were," you say. "Really bad. And you're doing it again tomorrow."
	<br><br>
	Robin stares at you, then laughs when <<he>> realises you're teasing <<him>>.
<<elseif $speech_attitude is "meek" or $speech_attitude is "shy">>
	"You stayed until the end," you say. "That's enough for your first day."
	<br><br>
	Robin looks back towards the counter before giving a small nod.
<<else>>
	"You were new," you say. "Tomorrow you'll know more than you did today."
	<br><br>
	Robin pulls a face, but <<he>> does not argue.
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Robin Cafe First Shift 4]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Robin Cafe First Shift 4
<<effects>>
Sam looks over from behind the counter. When Robin is not looking,
Sam gives you a small shrug and points towards <<him>>, as if to say that new staff often struggle on their first shift.
<br><br>
Robin got through the first shift.
<<npcincr Robin love 1>><<npcincr Robin trauma 2>><<glove>><<grtrauma>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Ocean Breeze]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: Robin Cafe Difficult
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "cafe">><<effects>>
<<person1>>
<<generates2>>
<<run ensureRobinCafe()>>
You've barely taken two steps into the cafe when you hear someone raising <<his>> voice at the counter.
A <<person2>><<person>> stands in front of Robin with a cup on the counter between them.
<br><br>
<<He>> points at the drink as <<he>> speaks.
"I asked for no milk. Twice! Did the till get it wrong, or did you?"
<br><br>
<<person1>>Robin stands behind the counter with both hands pressed against the wood.
<<He>> looks at the customer without answering, but Sam is in the kitchen with the door shut.
The people at two nearby tables have stopped talking and are watching the argument.
<br><br>
Robin still hasn't apologised. Usually, <<he>> would have done that already.
<br><br>
<<link [[Step in|Robin Cafe Difficult Step]]>><<pass 10>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Stay where you are|Robin Cafe Difficult Wait]]>><<pass 10>><</link>>
<br>

:: Robin Cafe Difficult Step
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "cafe">><<effects>>
<<run ensureRobinCafe()>>
<<set $robinCafe.handled to "player">>
<<set $robinCafe.stage to 4>>
Before Robin can answer, you step in beside <<him>> and take the cup from the customer.
<br><br>
"Sorry about that," you say. You empty the drink and make another one while <<he>> watches,
this time leaving out the milk.
<br><br>
The <<person2>><<person>> watches you finish the new drink before taking it from you.
<<He>> complains about the cafe's standards, then turns away and carries the cup to a table.
<<person1>>Robin stays beside you the whole time. <<He>> does not interrupt or try to take over.
<br><br>
Once the customer is gone, Robin looks down at <<his>> apron. <<He>> pulls the knot loose behind <<his>> back,
then ties it again more slowly.
<br><br>
"Thanks," <<he>> says.
<br><br>
<<He>> keeps <<his>> attention on the apron for another second before looking up.
"I think I could've handled that. I was trying to work out what to say."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Robin Cafe Difficult Step 2]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Robin Cafe Difficult Step 2
<<effects>>
<<if $speech_attitude is "bratty">>
	"You were taking your time about it," you say. The words are already out before you realise how they sound.
<<elseif $speech_attitude is "meek" or $speech_attitude is "shy">>
	"I'm sorry," you say. "I didn't think."
<<else>>
	"I know," you say. "I just didn't want you to have to deal with <<him>>."
<</if>>
<br><br>
Robin pulls <<his>> hands away from the apron. "That's the problem.
People keep stepping in because they don't want me to deal with things like that. I need to learn how to do it myself."
<br><br>
<<He>> picks up a cloth and walks over to an empty table. There are only a few crumbs on it,
but <<he>> wipes them away anyway.<<npcincr Robin dom -2>><<lldom>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Ocean Breeze]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: Robin Cafe Difficult Wait
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "cafe">><<effects>>
<<run ensureRobinCafe()>>
<<set $robinCafe.handled to "robin">>
<<set $robinCafe.stage to 4>>
You stay by the door instead of stepping in. Part of you wants to help, but you wait and let Robin handle it.
<br><br>
Robin takes the cup from <<person2>>the <<person>> without arguing.
"I'll make you another one. It'll take about a minute. You can sit down while you wait, or stay here.
Which do you want?"
<br><br>
<<person2>>The <<person>> starts to answer, then stops. <<He>> looks at the nearby chair, then back at Robin.
After a few seconds, <<he>> pulls the chair out and sits down.
<br><br>
Robin turns back to the counter and makes the drink again. When it's ready, <<person1>><<he>>
carries it over and places it in front of <<person2>>the <<person>>. "Here you go."
<br><br>
<<person1>><<He>> returns to the counter before <<person2>>the <<person>> can start another argument
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Robin Cafe Difficult Wait 2]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Robin Cafe Difficult Wait 2
<<effects>>
The people at the two nearby tables watch for another few seconds. When nothing else happens,
they turn back to their drinks and conversations.
<br><br>
<<person1>>You walk over to Robin. <<His>> hands shake slightly as <<he>> puts the used cup aside.
When <<he>> notices you looking, <<he>> lowers them behind the counter.
<br><br>
"I've watched Sam do that about ten times," <<he>> says. "You give them something to choose.
Then they have to think about the choice instead of shouting."
<br><br>
<<if $speech_attitude is "bratty">>
	"Look at you," you say. "Terrifying."
	<br><br>
	"Shut up," <<he>> says, smiling.
<<elseif $speech_attitude is "meek" or $speech_attitude is "shy">>
	"That was really good," you manage.
	<br><br>
	Robin looks down for a second. This time, <<he>> doesn't immediately deny it.
<<else>>
	"You didn't need me," you say.
	<br><br>
	Robin pauses before answering. "No," <<he>> says, sounding a little surprised by it too.
<</if>>
<<npcincr Robin dom 6>><<gggdom>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Ocean Breeze]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: Robin Cafe Decision
<<endevent>>
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "home">><<effects>>
<<npc Robin>><<person1>>
<<run ensureRobinCafe()>>
Robin takes a folded work schedule from <<his>> pocket. <<He>> looks down at it for a few seconds,
turning it over between <<his>> fingers without opening it.
"Sam asked if I want to keep working at the cafe... Properly this time. Not as a trial."
<br><br>
<<if $robinCafe.handled is "robin">>
	<<He>> rubs <<his>> thumb along the edge of the paper. "I keep thinking about that customer with the milk.
	I actually dealt with it myself."
	<br><br>
	<<He>> looks down at the schedule again.
	"I'm not used to that. Usually, when something goes wrong, I'm the one who needs help."
<<else>>
	<<He>> rubs <<his>> thumb along the edge of the paper. "I keep thinking about that customer with the milk.
	You handled it for me. That was kind of you. But afterwards,
	I kept thinking that I should've been able to deal with it myself."
<</if>>
<br><br>
Robin folds the schedule once more, making the crease sharper.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Robin Cafe Decision 2]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Robin Cafe Decision 2
<<effects>>
"The cafe is different from my stand," <<he>> says. "Sam gave me a chance there. The stand was something I started myself."
<br><br>
<<He>> holds the folded paper against <<his>> knee.
<br><br>
"I don't know if I should keep the job, or just go back to the stand."
<br><br>
<<link [[Tell <<him>> to keep the job|Robin Cafe Decision Keep]]>><<pass 10>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Tell <<him>> the stand is enough|Robin Cafe Decision Quit]]>><<pass 10>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Tell <<him>> it's <<his>> call|Robin Cafe Decision Own]]>><<pass 10>><</link>>
<br>

:: Robin Cafe Decision Keep
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "home">><<effects>>
<<run ensureRobinCafe()>>
<<set $robinCafe.stage to 5>><<set $robinCafe.ended to "kept">>
"Keep the café job," you say. "You can still run the stand on Saturday."
<br><br>
Robin looks down at the rota again. <<He>> reads through the empty shifts, then picks up a pen.
<br><br>
"I can work from five to seven, Monday to Friday," <<he>> says as <<he>> writes <<his>> name beside each shift.
"I'll keep Saturday and Sunday for the stand."
<br><br>
<<He>> finishes writing and puts the pen down. <<He>> looks over the rota once more before folding it.
"No one's ever asked me what I wanted to do before. They usually just tell me."
<<npcincr Robin love 2>><<npcincr Robin trauma -3>><<glove>><<llrtrauma>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Robin Cafe Decision Keep 2]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Robin Cafe Decision Keep 2
<<effects>>
<span class="green">Robin has decided to keep working at Ocean Breeze.</span>
 <br><br>
<<robinoptions>>

:: Robin Cafe Decision Quit
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "home">><<effects>>
<<run ensureRobinCafe()>>
<<set $robinCafe.stage to 5>><<set $robinCafe.ended to "quit">>
"You don't need to keep working at the cafe," you say. "You can spend that time on the stand instead."
<br><br>
Robin looks down at the folded work schedule in <<his>> hands. After a few seconds,
<<he>> places it on the desk without opening it. "I'll tell <<nnpc_him "Sam">> tomorrow.
<<nnpc_He "Sam">>'ll probably understand... <<nnpc_He "Sam">> usually does."
<br><br>
Robin turns towards the window, thinking about it before continuing.
<br><br>
"I'm still glad I worked there. I learned how to use the till, and I got better at dealing with angry customers.
I'll still know how to do those things even after I leave."<<npcincr Robin trauma -2>><<lrtrauma>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Robin Cafe Decision Quit 2]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Robin Cafe Decision Quit 2
<<effects>>
<span class="gold">Robin has left the cafe</span>, but keeps the skills <<he>> learned there.
<span class="blue">Robin now has more time to run the stand</span>, and <<he>> is better prepared to manage it.
<br><br>
<<robinoptions>>

:: Robin Cafe Decision Own
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "home">><<effects>>
<<run ensureRobinCafe()>>
<<set $robinCafe.stage to 5>>
"It's your name on the rota," you say. "Not mine."
<br><br>
Robin watches you, waiting for you to tell <<him>> what to do. When you say nothing else,
<<he>> looks back down at the paper.
<br><br>
<<if C.npc.Robin.dom gte 55 or $robinCafe.handled is "robin">>
	<<set $robinCafe.ended to "kept">>
	<<He>> unfolds the rota and reads it again.
	"I'm keeping the job. The money helps, obviously. But I want to stay too."
	<br><br>
	<<He>> picks up a pen and writes <<his>> name on the rota. <<He>> finishes without looking to you for approval.
	<<npcincr Robin dom 5>><<npcincr Robin trauma -4>><<ggdom>><<llrtrauma>>
	<br><br>
<<else>>
	<<set $robinCafe.ended to "quit">>
	Robin turns the folded rota over in <<his>> hands, then sets it down without opening it.
	"I don't want the job. I know I could keep doing it. But I've been spending more time there and less time at my stand."
	<br><br>
	<<He>> rests a hand on the rota. "The stand is mine. I don't want to keep neglecting it."
	<br><br>
	<<He>> pushes the rota aside. "I'll tell <<nnpc_him "Sam">> myself. I want to do that part."
	<<npcincr Robin dom 3>><<npcincr Robin trauma -2>><<gdom>><<lrtrauma>>
	<br><br>
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Robin Cafe Decision Own 2]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Robin Cafe Decision Own 2
<<effects>>
<<if $robinCafe.ended is "kept">>
	<span class="green">Robin decided to stay at the cafe.</span>
<<else>>
	<span class="green">Robin chose to focus on the stand.</span>
<</if>>
<<robinoptions>>

:: Robin Cafe Shortage
<<endevent>>
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "cafe">><<effects>>
<<npc Robin>><<person1>>
You step behind the counter and take the empty carton from Robin before <<he>> squeezes it any harder.
"Come with me," you say. "Just for a minute."
<br><br>
You lead <<him>> into the staff room and shut the door. Robin turns to you as soon as you are alone.
"We're out of $phase," <<he>> says. "I checked the fridge and the shelf next to the machine. There's none left."
<br><br>
<<He>> rubs <<his>> hands against <<his>> apron.
<br><br>
"I was supposed to tell Sam when we opened the last one. I didn't realise it was the last carton until just now."
<<He>> looks back towards the door. "People have already ordered drinks that need it. I don't know what to tell them."
<br><br>
<<link [[Help Robin calm down and work out what to do|Robin Cafe Shortage Reassure]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Cover the counter while Robin buys more|Robin Cafe Shortage Cover]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<if setup.inflation.canAfford(1000, "cafe")>>
	<<link [[Go and buy more yourself|Robin Cafe Shortage Fetch]]>><<money -1000 "cafe">><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>
<<if $chef_state gte 1>>
	<<link [[Use something else from the kitchen|Robin Cafe Shortage Substitute]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>

:: Robin Cafe Shortage Continue
<<endevent>>
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "cafe">><<effects>>
<<npc Robin>><<person1>>
You return to your tables. Several customers are still waiting for their orders,
so you keep working instead of stopping to help Robin.
<br><br>
Later, you pass the counter again and see Sam standing beside Robin.
